3763 |             assert_array_almost_equal(rank_proba, rank_score)\n3764 |         except AssertionError:\n3765 |             # Sometimes, the rounding applied on the probabilities will have\n3766 |             # ties that are not present in the scores because it is\n3767 |             # numerically more precise. In this case, we relax the test by\n3768 |             # grouping the decision function scores based on the probability\n3769 |             # rank and check that the score is monotonically increasing.\n3770 |             grouped_y_score = np.array(\n3771 |                 [b[rank_proba == group].mean() for group in np.unique(rank_proba)]\n3772 |             )\n3773 |             sorted_idx = np.argsort(grouped_y_score)\n3774 |             assert_array_equal(sorted_idx, np.arange(len(sorted_idx)))\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/feature_extraction/_hash.py:FeatureHasher.fit`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n128 | def fit(self, X=None, y=None):\n129 |         \"\"\"Only validates estimator's parameters.\n130 | \n131 |         This method allows to: (i) validate the estimator's parameters and\n132 |         (ii) be consistent with the scikit-learn transformer API.\n133 | \n134 |         Parameters\n135 |         ----------\n136 |         X : Ignored\n137 |             Not used, present here for API consistency by convention.\n138 | \n139 |         y : Ignored\n140 |             Not used, present here for API consistency by convention.\n141 | \n142 |         Returns\n143 |         -------\n144 |         self : object\n145 |             FeatureHasher class instance.\n146 |         \"\"\"\n147 |         return self\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"consistency\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/feature_extraction/text.py:HashingVectorizer.partial_fit`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n800 | def partial_fit(self, X, y=None):\n801 |         \"\"\"Only validates estimator's parame